---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { supportEmail } from '../config';
---

<Base
  title="Quiet Poker — Support"
  description="How to get help with Quiet Poker: a purchase that did not arrive, managing a subscription, and deleting your account and its data."
  prose
>
  <h1>Support</h1>

  <p class="lede">
    One person answers this address. Write in English if you can, and say what
    the app did and what you expected.
  </p>

  <p class="contact">
    <a href={`mailto:${supportEmail}`}>{supportEmail}</a>
  </p>

  <h2>A purchase that has not arrived</h2>
  <p>Almost always one of these three, in this order:</p>
  <ol>
    <li>
      <strong>Open the Shop tab and tap Restore purchases.</strong> A purchase
      that completed on another device, or before a reinstall, lands with this.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Check whether it is waiting for approval.</strong> With Ask to Buy,
      Apple holds the purchase until an approver responds, and the app says so.
      The chips arrive by themselves once it comes through &mdash; nothing needs
      doing here.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Write to us.</strong> Include the App Store order ID from the
      receipt Apple emailed you, the product you bought, and roughly when. That
      is enough to find the transaction and credit it.
    </li>
  </ol>

  <p>
    Payment itself is Apple&rsquo;s. Refunds are requested through
    <a href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com">reportaproblem.apple.com</a>, not
    through us &mdash; we never take the payment and cannot reverse it.
  </p>

  <h2>Managing or cancelling Plus</h2>
  <p>
    From the app: Shop tab, then <strong>Manage subscription</strong>. From the
    phone: Settings, your name, then Subscriptions. Cancelling stops the next
    renewal and leaves the period you have already paid for running to its end.
  </p>

  <h2 id="delete-account">Deleting your account and its data</h2>
  <p>
    In the app: <strong>Profile tab &rarr; Delete account</strong>. It removes
    the account and its chips for good, and it cannot be undone.
  </p>
  <p>
    The app will refuse while chips of yours are still in play &mdash; stand up
    from any table you are seated at, and close any private room you opened,
    then try again. This is so a deletion cannot strand the other players in a
    hand.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you cannot reach the app for some reason, write to
    <a href={`mailto:${supportEmail}`}>{supportEmail}</a> from the address on the
    account and ask for deletion. What is stored in the first place is listed in
    the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you only ever played offline, there is nothing to delete: offline play
    needs no account and sends nothing to a server. Removing the app removes it.
  </p>

  <h2>Reporting a bug</h2>
  <p>Useful in the message, in rough order of usefulness:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>What happened, and what you expected instead</li>
    <li>Whether it was an offline table, an online one, or outside a hand</li>
    <li>Your iPhone or iPad model and iOS version</li>
    <li>A screenshot, if the screen showed it</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Trouble signing in</h2>
  <p>
    Signing in uses Sign in with Apple. If it fails repeatedly, check that
    you are signed into an Apple Account on the device, and that the date and
    time are set automatically &mdash; a clock that is far out makes the
    sign-in fail in a way that looks like a rejection.
  </p>
  <p>
    You do not need an account to play offline. Signing in is what lets chips
    and a subscription follow you to another device, and what online tables
    need.
  </p>
</Base>

<style>
  .contact {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    margin-block: 1.5rem 0.5rem;
  }
</style>
